{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbnaStf4AcSqWfb8rLvM", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex for an ISO 8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`):\n\n```regex\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` is a four-digit year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` is a month from 01 to 12.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` is a day from 01 to 31.\n- `^\u2026$` anchors the match to the whole string. To find dates inside longer text, swap the anchors for `\\b`.\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01` and rejects `2026-13-01` and `2026-10-32`.\n\nIt doesn't check that the day exists in that month, so `2026-02-31` still matches. Regex can't handle that well, so validate those cases with a date parser. A leap-year-aware regex is possible but long."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7217, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7217}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f7838fbc-7290-42a2-ae6b-bbf6b4fc8289", "uuid": "dbd8cea8-1f6f-4f26-874b-84e0175d8210", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T15:53:20.667Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbnaScXqRpTHtHEsrcHk"}
